    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a foreign language to me—rigid and unyielding. I managed to scrape by in school, but it never clicked. My mind wanders to philosophy or literature instead; numbers just don’t inspire the same curiosity. It’s frustrating because I know it’s useful, but I can’t shake the feeling that I’m missing something fundamental. Maybe that’s why I avoid it now.",
